# Source-derived semantics

- The zero-sized parent carries `background-image: url("support/green_box.png")`; the 100px child has a red fallback and `background-image: inherit`.
- The assertion requires the inherited green image to cover the child, leaving one green square and no red.

# Compatibility adjustments

- Source IDs and tested declarations are preserved on nested Lynx `<view>` elements.
- Visible text uses a wrapping outer `<text>`, nested bold text, and an explicit ordinary U+0020 before the bold phrase.
- Content-box sizing and explicit body/paragraph spacing reproduce Web setup without relying on Lynx margin collapse.
- The card-local `green_box.png` is copied byte-for-byte from the pinned, reference-clean source cache.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- Lynx documents `background-image`, local URL images, `inherit`, fixed px geometry, and backgrounds on `<view>`.
- Three final-device runs are byte-stable failures at 3.5807%: WebView paints the inherited green image, while Lynx leaves the red fallback visible.
- Direct URL loading succeeds in the sibling `background-image-002` case, isolating this failure to inheritance rather than asset loading. The original Web test matches its pinned official reference exactly.
